644 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (As our designing progressed, we became more focused on evaluating the practicality of different mechanisms rather than simply their potential performance. We considered factors such as reliability, complexity and how each mechanism contributed to our competition strategy.)
/E (As our designing progressed, we became more focused on evaluating the practicality of different mechanisms rather than simply their potential performance. We considered factors such as reliability, complexity and how each mechanism contributed to our competition strategy.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
645 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (One major discussion involved choosing between a single lane and double lane pollen shooter. Although a double lane design could potentially increase shooting speed and decrease indexing area, but it also introduced greater complexity, maintenance and potential reliability issues. We ultimately selected a single lane hooded shooter because it offered greater accuracy, consistency and simplicity within our timeframe.)
/E (One major discussion involved choosing between a single lane and double lane pollen shooter. Although a double lane design could potentially increase shooting speed and decrease indexing area, but it also introduced greater complexity, maintenance and potential reliability issues. We ultimately selected a single lane hooded shooter because it offered greater accuracy, consistency and simplicity within our timeframe.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
646 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (We also explored improvements to our intake system, including the use of vector wheels to improve pollen collection. Additionally, we considered a ramp mechanism that could prevent pollen from spilling out while potentially obstructing opponents' shooting paths. This encouraged us to think beyond individual functions and consider how mechanisms could serve multiple purposes in the competition. )
/E (We also explored improvements to our intake system, including the use of vector wheels to improve pollen collection. Additionally, we considered a ramp mechanism that could prevent pollen from spilling out while potentially obstructing opponents' shooting paths. This encouraged us to think beyond individual functions and consider how mechanisms could serve multiple purposes in the competition. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
647 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Our drivetrain concepts also evolved as we considered the advantages and disadvantages of mecanum and swerve drive. We recognised the trade offs between manoeuvrability, mechanical complexity and reliability, placing greater importance on developing a stable and effective system rather than introducing unnecessary features.)
/E (Our drivetrain concepts also evolved as we considered the advantages and disadvantages of mecanum and swerve drive. We recognised the trade offs between manoeuvrability, mechanical complexity and reliability, placing greater importance on developing a stable and effective system rather than introducing unnecessary features.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
