836 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 89 0 R
/T (Pocketing was used on the drivebase plates to remove excess material and decrease weight. This makes our robot faster and lighter. We made the mistake of not having a solid channel through the middle of the robot, which caused the ball to get stuck inside the pocketing of the bottom plate. To fix this, we added a long plastic sheet, allowing the ball to move through smoothly. For our wheels, we calculated the optimal belt and pulley ratios for the right balance between speed and torque. )
/E (Pocketing was used on the drivebase plates to remove excess material and decrease weight. This makes our robot faster and lighter. We made the mistake of not having a solid channel through the middle of the robot, which caused the ball to get stuck inside the pocketing of the bottom plate. To fix this, we added a long plastic sheet, allowing the ball to move through smoothly. For our wheels, we calculated the optimal belt and pulley ratios for the right balance between speed and torque. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
