/P 89 0 R
/T (Our mark 1 robot was purely a drivebase without consideration of the other systems, allowing us to test our wheels. Mark 2 drivebase had roughly the right parameters and wheel locations, however we did not have pocketing and proper spacers, which reduced its structural integrity and made it harder to wire.)
/E (Our mark 1 robot was purely a drivebase without consideration of the other systems, allowing us to test our wheels. Mark 2 drivebase had roughly the right parameters and wheel locations, however we did not have pocketing and proper spacers, which reduced its structural integrity and made it harder to wire.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [16]
>>
