<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 93 0 R
/T (The robot will continuously reference the precalculated table to adjust the shooter RPM and hood angle. Once the RPM is within approximately 50 of the target and the hood angle is within 2 degrees, it activates the indexer to begin shooting. It also adjusts its rotation to oppose its tangent velocity, compensating for sideways movement so the ball maintains its intended trajectory into the hive. The driver retains control of the robot's movement while the shooting system automatically adjusts to the required settings.)
/E (The robot will continuously reference the precalculated table to adjust the shooter RPM and hood angle. Once the RPM is within approximately 50 of the target and the hood angle is within 2 degrees, it activates the indexer to begin shooting. It also adjusts its rotation to oppose its tangent velocity, compensating for sideways movement so the ball maintains its intended trajectory into the hive. The driver retains control of the robot's movement while the shooting system automatically adjusts to the required settings.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
